    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, PARTLY-STALE] Reviewed 2026-11-01 at dev 100b6fbb6e. WI-dibuf (d3bbf8bdcf, 2026-10-31) added *Test/*Tests/*IT for .java/.kt/.scala and *Tests.swift. Live probe now True: src/com/x/FooTest.java, FooTests/FooTests.swift, src/FooIT.java, androidTest/.../FooTest.kt (by its name only). Still False: MyApp.Tests/FooTests.cs, MyApp.UnitTests/FooTests.cs, src/FooTests.cs, src/FooSpec.scala, src/FooSpec.kt, androidTest/java/Helper.kt, src/FooTest.groovy. sketch.TEST_FILE_PATTERNS is now defined but never referenced (dead data); supply_chain keeps its own TEST_FILE_PATTERNS. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\npaths.classify_test_file (the shared is_test_file chokepoint, also used by sketch._analyze_test_files to count test files) recognises snake/kebab test names (test_*, *_test.*, *.test.*, *.spec.*) and test directories, but not the PascalCase-suffix conventions of the JVM/.NET/Swift/Scala ecosystems outside a tests/ or src/test/ directory. Live probe (2026-10-07, dev @ e3f091d458):\n  src/com/x/FooTest.java -> False\n  MyApp.Tests/FooTests.cs -> False      (dotted *.Tests / *.UnitTests project dirs are the .NET convention)\n  MyApp.UnitTests/FooTests.cs -> False\n  app/src/androidTest/java/FooTest.kt -> False   (Android instrumentation tests)\n  FooTests/FooTests.swift -> False\n  src/FooSpec.scala -> False\n  (control) src/test/kotlin/FooTest.kt -> True\nEffect: such files count as production in the sketch's \"N non-test + M test\" line and are not deprioritised as test code in ranking/slices; the sketch's test-framework detection (WI-vosag: xunit/nunit/mstest/XCTest/kotlin.test patterns) never sees them, so a .NET repo with tests in MyApp.Tests/ reports no test files and no framework. sketch.TEST_FILE_PATTERNS already lists *Test.java / *Tests.java, so the knowledge exists in a second place that classify_test_file does not use (L53: one classifier). Fix shape: add filename rules for [A-Z]\\w*(Test|Tests|Spec|IT)\\.(java|kt|cs|swift|scala|groovy) (case-sensitive capital T to avoid 'Latest.java'/'Contest.java') and directory rules for *.Tests / *.UnitTests / *.IntegrationTests / androidTest; mind the breadth trade-offs documented on is_test_file (WI-popok KEEP verdict) and measure the ranking/tier delta on a JVM and a .NET repo before merging. Found while fixing WI-vosag."  # 88bc
